summary: Named mf_ignore presets: apply/replace/remove them on a directory (default: list). The target directory is chosen with -d <path> (default: the repository root)

!! Reference

```
Named mf_ignore presets: apply/replace/remove them on a directory (default: list). The target directory is chosen with -d <path> (default: the repository root)

Usage: mf ignore [COMMAND]

Commands:
  add     Append the presets' patterns to the target's mf_ignore set
  remove  Remove the presets' patterns from the target's mf_ignore set
  set     Replace the target's whole mf_ignore set with the presets' patterns (with no preset, clears the set)
  list    List the available presets (with -d, also the target's active patterns)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
```
